Lizzy: eh, we sort of had a falling out.
Juniper: What? You didn’t tell us anything.
Lizzy: he said something about werewolves and vampires not working out together and the vanished dramatically. It’s really hard to end a conversation on the high ground with that guy.
Barb: So he’s potentially available?
Lizzy: Ew. Don’t even think about it.
Noah: Your last boyfriend ended up being a shapeshifter, Barb. I thought that would’ve thrown you off supernatural creatures.
Barb: I’m sorry for being human, okay?
Lizzy: It’s been a whole week and a bit since anything weird has happened, and it’s driving me crazy. Usually some, like, portal would open up somewhere and a demon would come out and eat a baby.
Barb: You want a demon to eat a baby? God, you’re sick in the head.
Lizzy: I don’t WANT a demon to eat a baby but at least then I wouldn’t be waiting for it to happen. And I know how to deal with demons.
Juniper: Sometimes things don’t happen, and that can be scarier than things happening.
Lizzy: Something always happens! Ever since I got bitten by the mayor who was secretly a werewolf.
Noah: I still can’t believe he came from a long line of werewolves with a long family history of protecting Vermilion Hills. I guess that’s why he had such good polling numbers.
Lizzy: When I held him in my arms as he died and he told me it was my job now, and then Valerie showed up and told me that I was part of this prophecy…
Barb: Are you going to tell us you want to run for mayor? Because I could totally help with your campaign. I actually have a few ideas. You will have to reinvent every part of your personality, though.
Juniper: I don’t think that would make you a very good campaign manager.
Lizzy: I’m not running for Mayor. I’m saying that it’s a lot of responsibility to have the fate of the entire living world on my shoulders.
Juniper: We’re all here for you, Lizzy. You aren’t saving the world alone. And King Fear died super easily, so the rest of the vampire lords are probably going to be swiss cheese pretty soon.
Lizzy: But half of you are leaving to go to Emmerdale, and Noah’s taking a gap year, and I’ll be stuck in some class I don’t even want to take.
Barb: You could still try and get into Emmerdale’s regular admission period. It opens up next month, I double checked.
Lizzy: No. Valerie said I shouldn’t leave the town. It’s too risky.
Barb: That’s so unfair!
