Everyone: …
Lizzy: What? ? You didn’t get in?
Barb: Bullshit.
Juniper: No, I got the rejection letter this morning. I’m not bummed about it or anything, I didn’t really want to go. It’s too “establishment” for me.
Lizzy: I’m sorry.
Lizzy: [V.O] This is awesome!
Lizzy: Are you going to go to VCR instead?
Juniper: Yeah, I was thinking about it.
Barb: That sucks. Now I’m going to be all alone! All my new friends are going to be clowns, literally!
Lizzy: Wait, sorry, say that again?
Barb: I didn’t tell you guys because I was sort of embarrassed, but I got into the clown program.
Noah: No way. You’re going to become a clown?
Barb: Clowns are very important to society and have a strict code in which they operate. But no, I don’t want to become a clown. I’m going to become an actor.
Lizzy: Uh, how does becoming a clown make you an actor?
Barb: They’re not a lot of jobs I hollywood right now for traditional roles, so I’m going to go for the ones that have a gap in the market.
Juniper: Which means?
Barb: Zombies, scary ghosts, creepy ghouls. I figure I have enough experience with the real things to sell it.
Noah: Wow, Barb. I knew you were a horror movie nut, but I didn’t think you’d go so far to become part of the industry. I’m impressed.
Barb: Your approval means nothing to me.
No: yeah, I know. Still impressed.
Barb: thanks.
Lizzy: We can all send each other electronic emails or chat on MySpace. And you could visit on your breaks, right?
Barb: I guess. Ugh. It’s so hard to chase your dreams.
Lizzy: By the way, my mom offered to drive all of us tomorrow, if you want.
Barb: I’m still taking my Limo. If my dress is ruined, I’ll just have to make due in other ways.
Noah: I’ll take that ride.
Juniper: My too. Saves me from having to walk.
Lizzy: Okay, see you all bright and early.

Lizzy: hey, Juniper. I am really sorry you didn’t get in. I know it meant a lot to you.
